{"title":"2001 IMO Shortlist Problems/A3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/f/78f4154c6fecbabd6ef24a6d28cc3eb465831cd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2, \\dotsc, x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"11\" /> be arbitrary real numbers.  Prove the inequality\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/a/44a956c293c833ce8f4a5508fbeba144a7abdcd4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x_1}{1+x_1^2} + \\frac{x_2}{1+x_1^2 + x_2^2} + \\dotsb + \\frac{x_n}{1+ x_1^2  + \\dotsb + x_n^2} &lt; \\sqrt{n} .\\]\" width=\"424\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We prove the following general inequality, for arbitrary positive real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/f/80f3e7f2cb0a7ce2bf33912680f2c3a6809657ed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{j=1}^n \\frac{x_j}{k^2 + \\sum_{i=1}^j x_i^2} \\le \\sqrt{n}/k ,\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"49\" />\nwith equality only when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/02349576cee613512cdf301a365f06c0760acab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>We proceed by induction on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.  For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/02349576cee613512cdf301a365f06c0760acab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, we have trivial equality.  Now, suppose our inequality holds for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.  Then by inductive hypothesis,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/1/83117c498a01be7727464f61c42cdad6b5549cdc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{j=1}^{n+1} \\frac{x_j}{k^2 + \\sum_{i=1}^j x_i^2} = \\frac{x_1}{k^2 + x_1^2} + \\sum_{j=2}^{n+1} \\frac{x_j}{k^2 + x_1^2 + \\sum_{i=2}^j x_i^2} \\le \\frac{x_1}{k^2 + x_1^2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{n}}{\\sqrt{k^2 + x_1^2}} .\\]\" width=\"591\" height=\"52\" />\nIf we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6ccb67cac5420a80b9b4165545284c711c3f634f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t= \\text{Arcsin} \\left(x_1/\\sqrt{x_1^2 +k^2} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"201\" height=\"32\" />, then we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb5173bbb2f29e798d9b5ef43248bc225339f9c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x_1}{k^2 + x_1^2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{n}}{\\sqrt{k^2+x_1^2}} = (\\sin t \\cos t + \\sqrt{n} \\cos t)/k \\le (\\lvert \\sin t \\rvert + \\sqrt{n} \\cos t)/k ,\\]\" width=\"537\" height=\"46\" />\nwith equality only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7542f5966180deb46f340b6d5ebe8fe47e52cb4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos t= \\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"80\" height=\"12\" />.\nBy the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cauchy-Schwarz_Inequality\" title=\"Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality\">Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality</a>,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/a/0ea86e87951ffeaa992851b72d21921ec4353e61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\lvert \\sin t \\rvert + \\sqrt{n} \\cos t)/k \\le (1 + n)^{1/2}(\\sin^2 t + \\cos^2 t)^{1/2}/k = \\sqrt{n+1}/k,\\]\" width=\"498\" height=\"20\" />\nwith equality only when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/8/5582de892b2cf60f94bf0b73ab2c921d77006197.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\lvert \\sin t \\rvert, \\cos t) = (1/\\sqrt{n^2+1}, n/\\sqrt{n^2+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"305\" height=\"21\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d0700437258eac3c3675350a4aa0976bfd707d57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lvert n/\\sqrt{n^2+1} \\right\\rvert &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"129\" height=\"33\" />, our equality cases never coincide, so we have the desired strict inequality for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />.  Thus our inequality is true by induction.  The problem statement therefore follows from setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cauchy-Schwarz_Inequality\" title=\"Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality\">Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality</a>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/d/0bd2d2f1cdd44a1a5cdb52c27e8734695303e37b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+a_2+.....+a_k \\leq \\sqrt{n}.\\sqrt{a_1^2+a_2^2+................+a_k^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"418\" height=\"35\" />\nFor all real numbers. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1abb8e46a3e1702b74a7295f7d93961403318c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,....$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" />  \nHence it is only required to prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7bea8e9a9c49bb09cd37f6938b30858f7711045.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1^2+a_2^2+................+a_k^2&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"235\" height=\"21\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/a/63a1f8d703254913f48ff25f65e25397a76b520d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k=\\dfrac{x_k}{1+x_1^2+... x_k^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"153\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84c0da6f9bb05c6b3f2db89eea12691e4b79066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/c/3bceac1f4eb7c5bccfd94419cae8a6464d31b931.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k^2=(\\dfrac{x_k}{1+x_1^2+... x_k^2})^2 &lt; \\dfrac{x_k^2}{(1+x_1^2+... x_{k-1}^2)(1+x_1^2+... x_k^2)} = \\dfrac{1}{1+x_1^2+... x_{k-1}^2}-\\dfrac{1}{1+x_1^2+... x_k^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"740\" height=\"47\" /> \n</p><p>For k=1, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/3/3a3d5f349ec8ea1dd12559326d421db18fb020f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1^2 = 1-\\dfrac{1}{1+x_1^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"128\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Summing these inequalities, the right-hand side yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/6/3268c8153b020cb35d49af4a4f6bb02f100dbd10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{n=1}^{k}a_n^2\\leq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"83\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p>Hence Proved by Maths1234RC \nP.S. This is my first solution on AOPS.<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/9/a493ed62810b72e88e199643a3a3413c570311f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n = 1 + x^2 + \\cdots + x_n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"180\" height=\"21\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/7/f675d9046ad252aca136cf3559eb894946a274d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_0 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> by convention.\n</p><p>Rewriting the inequality,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/45560a44bb989d9766ead6ad1b9bf81b2f93d50f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x_1}{S_1} + \\frac{x_2}{S_2} + \\cdots + \\frac{x_n}{S_n} &lt; \\sqrt{n}\\]\" width=\"206\" height=\"35\" />\nmust be proven.\n</p><p>Note that by Chebyshev's inequality, the following could be driven.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/436be9f2868e10ed843664373b2cdc00715ddd95.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left( \\sum_{i = 1}^n \\frac{x_i}{S_i} \\right)^2 \\leq n \\left( \\sum_{i = 1}^n \\frac{x_i^2}{S_i^2} \\right)\\]\" width=\"195\" height=\"57\" />\nTherefore, it suffices to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/2/e5298140a3f1910c69f30cb0b3e2ee0ad89d47ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i = 1}^n \\frac{x_i^2}{S_i^2} &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"87\" height=\"53\" />. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/1/e319d9f951ceca34ba3ba84948ae5513ee0924fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i^2 = S_i - S_{i - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n<pre> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/9/b09cc674c154fb1e364c6555b853018ff1f49021.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Lemma.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" />\n <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/669aeb67ef31cb10b4c8f5570f654532c8fdd900.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i = 1}^n \\frac{S_i - S_{i - 1}}{S_i^2} &lt; 1\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"47\" />\n is true.\n</pre>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/a/9daac4410faa90487c839bbc058df74907d0a567.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Proof.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74a070eea97d9363f58a257e05e75fc69efa753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> is a monotonically increasing sequence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/1/6213d79eb602babad92862e6bc5a503ec802e212.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_i^2 \\geq S_i \\cdot S_{i - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"21\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/b/82b77f7edbea7b5ea8a0aac0177187cb58987ba2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i = 1}^n \\frac{S_i - S_{i - 1}}{S_i^2} \\leq \\sum_{i = 1}^n \\frac{S_i - S_{i - 1}}{S_i \\cdot S_{i - 1}} = \\sum_{i = 1}^n \\left( \\frac{1}{S_{i - 1}} - \\frac{1}{S_i} \\right) = \\frac{1}{S_0} - \\frac{1}{S_n} = 1 - \\frac{1}{S_n} &lt; 1\\]\" width=\"583\" height=\"47\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Hence, the inequality is true.\n</p><p>~MaPhyCom (Thinking Tree)\n</p><p>I also have a video explanation of this solution!!\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mjUccETe65w\">Please consider subscribing&#160;:))</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A3&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems\" title=\"2001 IMO Shortlist Problems\">2001 IMO Shortlist Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mathlinks.ro/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=119163#p119163\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018045029\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 223/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 353/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8477/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.707      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    6.707      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6093:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018045029 and revision id 261478. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}